# .trivyignore — Accepted CVE suppressions for maternal-system
#
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNNN [# comment]
# Each entry is reviewed quarterly. CVEs are suppressed only when:
#   1. The vulnerable code path is not reachable in this deployment, OR
#   2. No fix is available AND exploitability score < 4.0 (CVSS v3 Low)
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-10
# Reviewer: Security Engineering

# ── Node.js toolchain / build-time only ────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2022-25883  semver <7.5.2 — ReDoS in range parsing.
# Only present as a transitive devDep (typescript, tsx). Never in production bundle.
CVE-2022-25883

# CVE-2023-26136  tough-cookie <4.1.3 — prototype pollution.
# Transitive via jest/vitest test runner deps. Not reachable at runtime.
CVE-2023-26136

# CVE-2023-44270  postcss <8.4.31 — line return parsing.
# Transitive via vite in apps/web. Build-time only; not deployed.
CVE-2023-44270

# ── PostgreSQL client ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2021-3749  axios <0.21.2 — ReDoS in url normalisation.
# Transitive via africastalking SDK. Africastalking only makes outbound
# requests to fixed AT endpoints — no user-controlled URL input.
CVE-2021-3749

# ── Container base image ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CVE-2023-4863  libwebp — heap buffer overflow.
# Fixed in node:20-alpine3.18+. Pin Dockerfile to node:20.11-alpine3.19 or later.
# Tracked in: https://github.com/.../issues/NNN
# Uncomment below once Dockerfiles are pinned:
# CVE-2023-4863
